{# goal: Produce the program-manager closeout report: the functional outcome, open items with closure state, and the banked learning. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    goal_text: string
    functional_outcome: string
    change_summary: string
    decisions: array
    open_items: array
    validation: array
    learning: string
  output:
    report: string
---

{# Phase 5 — Closeout report: the program manager's report to the product
   manager. Functional outcome first; open items named; learning banked. #}
Produce the closeout report with this structure:

## Outcome
{{ functional_outcome }}
What the operator can now do, or what no longer breaks — in the
operator's terms, tied to the goal: "{{ goal_text }}"

## What changed
{{ change_summary }}
Technical summary, each item tied to the part of the goal it serves.
Files by project-relative path.

## Validation
{% if validation %}
| Command | Observed output | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
{% for item in validation %}
| `{{ item.command }}` | {{ item.observed_output | replace("\n", " ") }} | {{ item.verdict }} |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No validation records were supplied; verification is **not run**, not passed.
{% endif %}

## Open items
{% if open_items %}
| # | Item | Closure state | Owner |
|---|------|---------------|-------|
{% for item in open_items %}
| {{ item[0] }} | {{ item[1] }} | {{ item[2] }} | {{ item[3] }} |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
None exist (searched and verified clean).
{% endif %}
Found-but-not-fixed, blocked verifications, parallel-stream hazards.
Each entry is a flat list `["<id>", "<title>", "<state>", "owner:<owner>"]`
with `state` in `{fixed-verified, delegated-tracked, operator-decision, reported-abandoned}`
and `owner` in `{self, sub-agent:<label>, operator, none}`.
An empty list must mean "none exist", not "none looked for".

## Decisions recorded
{% if decisions %}
| Decision | Where persisted |
|---|---|
{% for d in decisions %}
| {{ d[0] }} | {{ d[1] }} |
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
None were recorded this cycle.
{% endif %}
Ratifications, supersessions, spec recoveries — with where they were
persisted (curator memory id / doc path). Each entry is a flat list
`["<decision>", "<curator memory id | doc path>"]`. An empty list must
mean "none were recorded", not "none were looked for".

## Learning banked
{{ learning }}
One sentence the next bit of work starts from.
